<div id="pg-scenarios" class="page">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="part-badge">Part B · Section 3</div>
    <h2>Real Screening Call Scenarios</h2>
    <p>Three scenarios you will face every day. Know the exact question and the exact response for each. Practice until these are automatic.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="content-wrap">

    <div class="callout gold">
      <div class="callout-icon">🎯</div>
      <div class="callout-body">
        <h4>The Universal First Question — Never Skip This</h4>
        <p><strong>"Can you confirm your work authorisation status?"</strong><br>This is the first compliance question on every call, before you go any further. Work auth comes after a brief pitch and interest check — but BEFORE the full skill qualification. If the candidate is not authorised for the role, the subsequent conversation is wasted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Scenario A -->
    <div class="scenario opta">
      <div class="scenario-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Scenario A — Candidate says: "I'm on OPT"</h3>
          <p>The most time-sensitive work auth situation. Expiry tracking is everything.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scen-badge">OPT</div>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-body">
        <div class="ask-block">
          <h4>Ask These Questions</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Is it standard OPT or STEM OPT?</li>
            <li>What is your EAD expiry date?</li>
            <li>Have you applied for H-1B this cycle?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="say-block">Great — this req is W-2 compatible with OPT. I just need to confirm your EAD covers the full contract duration. Your EAD expires [date] and this contract runs [X months] — does that timeline work for you?</div>
        <div class="flag-block">EAD expires before contract ends. H-1B lottery is pending and OPT gap (cap-gap) may apply — candidate could be forced to stop work mid-contract.</div>
        <div class="action-block">If EAD covers the contract → proceed. If borderline (within 2 months) → flag to manager before submitting. Never submit an OPT candidate whose EAD expires before the contract ends.</div>

        <h4 style="margin-top:20px;font-size:13px;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;">Expiry Check Logic</h4>
        <div class="formula" style="font-size:13px;">
          <span class="comment">// The contract duration check:</span><br>
          Contract start date + Contract duration = Expected end date<br>
          EAD expiry must be &gt; Expected end date<br><br>
          <span class="comment">// Example (safe):</span><br>
          Start: Jan 1, 2025 + 6 months = <span class="highlight">End: July 1, 2025</span><br>
          EAD expiry: <span class="highlight">Dec 15, 2025</span> → ✓ EAD covers contract period<br><br>
          <span class="comment">// Example (dangerous — DO NOT SUBMIT without flagging):</span><br>
          Start: Jan 1, 2025 + 6 months = <span class="highlight">End: July 1, 2025</span><br>
          EAD expiry: <span class="highlight">May 10, 2025</span> → ✗ EAD expires mid-contract
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Scenario B -->
    <div class="scenario h1bscen">
      <div class="scenario-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Scenario B — Candidate says: "I'm on H-1B"</h3>
          <p>The most nuanced scenario. Check the job order FIRST before saying anything else.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scen-badge">H1B</div>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-body">
        <div class="ask-block">
          <h4>Ask These Questions (After Checking Job Order)</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Who is your current H-1B sponsor?</li>
            <li>Are you open to an H-1B transfer?</li>
            <li>What is your I-94 / H-1B approval expiry date?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="say-block">I understand. Let me check the job order — [check]. Unfortunately this client has specified no H-1B transfers at this time. I'd love to keep you in mind for roles that do accept H-1B. Can I add you to our database?</div>
        <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-light);margin:8px 0 8px;font-style:italic;">(If H-1B IS accepted by this client:) "An H-1B transfer is possible — I'll flag this with my manager to confirm the client's process and timeline before we go further."</p>
        <div class="flag-block">Req says "No H-1B". Transfer takes 3–8 weeks minimum — client may not be willing to wait even if work auth is technically compatible.</div>
        <div class="action-block">Check job order FIRST. If No H-1B → end professionally and offer to keep in database. If H-1B allowed → flag to manager before proceeding. Never promise a transfer timeline to the candidate.</div>
        <div class="callout warn" style="margin-top:16px;">
          <div class="callout-icon">💬</div>
          <div class="callout-body">
            <h4>Why "I'd keep you in mind" Matters</h4>
            <p>The phrase "I'd love to keep you in mind for roles that accept H-1B" keeps the relationship alive without making a false promise. H-1B candidates are often highly qualified — you may have a role for them in the future. Add them to your database and tag their work auth correctly in Ceipal.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Scenario C -->
    <div class="scenario gcscen">
      <div class="scenario-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Scenario C — Candidate says: "I'm a Green Card holder"</h3>
          <p>The cleanest work auth outcome. Proceed quickly — GC candidates are in demand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scen-badge">GC</div>
      </div>
